#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"इतने जानवरों और दोस्तों के लिए हमारा घर बहुत छोटा है! फ्रॉस्टटॉर्प से बारह लट्ठे, औज़ारों की दो "
"पेटियाँ और तारकोल के दो घड़े लाओ, और हम इसे लंबा कर देंगे।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "बारह लट्ठे! अपनी बड़ी नाव भर लो।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "कुल्हाड़ियाँ और कीलें। अब छत के लिए तारकोल।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr "पड़ोसियों के साथ रात भर ठक-ठक... हमारा लंबा घर अब दुगना लंबा है! दावत के लिए जगह।"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr "लंबे घर के आख़िर में एक हिस्सा जोड़कर उसे और लंबा किया जा सकता था, रेलगाड़ी की तरह।"

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "हरी घाटी"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"तुमने पूरे साल मेरी घाटी की मदद की। तुम्हारे फ़ार्म के पीछे वाली हरी घाटी का कोई मालिक नहीं है: "
"देवताओं की दावत के लिए मुझे कपड़े की दो पेटियाँ और शहद की दो पेटियाँ लाओ, और वह तुम्हारी।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "सभा-भवन के लिए कपड़ा। अब शहद।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "पिताजी थिंग सभा में सबके सामने कहते हैं: हरी घाटी इल्वा और सिग्रिड की है!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "थिंग सभा में, जो आज़ाद लोगों की बैठक थी, ज़मीन और क़ानूनों के फ़ैसले होते थे।"

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "घाटी के लिए मधुमक्खियाँ"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"घाटी तिपतिया घास और हीदर से भरी है। मधुमक्खियों को यह बहुत पसंद आएगा! फ़ार्म पर तीन छत्ते रखो, और "
"हमारे पास साल भर शहद रहेगा।"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "भुन, भुन, भुन! घाटी में तीन छत्ते। हमारे लिए शहद, और शहद-शराब के लिए भी।"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
